    "created_at": "2026-11-09T21:21:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-09T21:21:52Z",
    "body": "Reopened: the maintainer still sees this broken on main (2026-11-09).\n\n**What happens:** \"Lay on plane\" with a picked face does not rotate the model so the face lies on the chosen plane. It only **moves** the model down until it sits below/on the plane. With Z up and the plane being the floor in a G17 orientation, a face that isn't already facing down stays tilted, so this isn't \"face to plane\".\n\n**Also seen:** changing the part alignment by hand roughly works, but it shifts the model relative to the origin point, so it isn't a true face-to-plane either.\n\n**Expected:** the picked face's outward normal is rotated onto the plane's normal (G17: the face lies flat on the floor, normal pointing -Z, part above), the model is then translated so the face lies in the plane, and the part keeps its relationship to the origin as the setup's alignment defines it, without a stray shift. Undo restores the previous placement.\n\n**Done means:** a test lays a face that starts tilted (e.g. 30 degrees off) onto G17 and asserts the face normal is -Z and the face plane is z = 0 afterwards, with the part above it; the same for G18/G19; and the part-alignment edit no longer shifts the model off its origin reference.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
